{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"39ccb6d5be2ed3929bdc1e0e89ab1542445607e09301326b6df5a88e137e13cc","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T15:36:11Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_recovered_from":"94579e79ac30d11ff40723765dc8be9ec4ad94161e21a853659465ca1a382515","anchor_verified":true,"mapped_intervals":[[331,333]],"mapped_path":"scripts/packed-smoke.mjs","quoted_text":"    const child = spawn(bin, [JSON.stringify(manifest)], {\n      stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n    });","reason":"The smoke creates an isolated install prefix and temporary workspace, but `mcpSmoke(prefix, ...)` calls `mcpRoundTrip` without the prefix and `mcpRoundTrip` spawns the MCP bin with no `cwd`. The child therefore inherits the caller's cwd (e.g. the checkout), so startup-time config/path resolution can depend on the source tree instead of the isolated consumer prefix. This is a concrete isolation defect in the current test harness, not merely a request for a new requirement.","recovered_anchor":{"anchor_recovered_from":"94579e79ac30d11ff40723765dc8be9ec4ad94161e21a853659465ca1a382515","blob":"28bac081f95f0e8adbcf3296d13180bc5093907d","intervals":[[331,333]],"path":"scripts/packed-smoke.mjs"},"target":"9046411c2e8bb60070deaf747d5d95c7a3244d01"},"finding_id":"65771679be15d65a5eeb401ee10e8dc46dd9f998bf20565942886a761763759c","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"b1e0cb2ef3bd136755adc1d05ce48052c8662f0ff48ce0781aab9a39888418a8"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:65771679be15d65a5eeb401ee10e8dc46dd9f998bf20565942886a761763759c:0ad3730939fed4fddbf72bf03462fbe8520015fbec65b3d948f7795cd51405a2"}